# Example local Bazel overrides for rules_bdeg.
#
# Copy to "user.bazelrc" (untracked) and adapt. The project .bazelrc picks it
# up automatically via `try-import %workspace%/user.bazelrc`.
#
# Nothing here is required to build the project. These are escape hatches for
# restricted networks, custom CA trust stores and local caches. Do NOT commit
# your user.bazelrc - it is environment-specific and may reveal internal
# infrastructure.

# --- TLS trust store --------------------------------------------------------
# Needed when your network terminates TLS with an internal CA, which makes
# Bazel's module fetches fail with:
#   PKIX path building failed: unable to find valid certification path
# Point Bazel's embedded JVM at a trust store that contains your CA.
# ("changeit" is the stock JDK default trust store password, not a secret.)
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStore=/etc/ssl/certs/java/cacerts
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Djavax.net.ssl.trustStorePassword=changeit

# Repository rules shell out to curl/python, which use their own CA bundles.
# common --repo_env=SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
# common --repo_env=CURL_CA_BUNDLE=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt
# common --repo_env=REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt

# --- HTTP(S) proxy ----------------------------------------------------------
# Replace the placeholder host/port with your own. Keep loopback out of proxy
# handling so the Bazel client can still reach its own server.
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttp.proxyHost=proxy.example.com
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttp.proxyPort=8080
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttps.proxyHost=proxy.example.com
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttps.proxyPort=8080
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dhttp.nonProxyHosts=localhost|127.0.0.1|127.*|[::1]
# common --repo_env=NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1

# --- Networking / timeouts --------------------------------------------------
# Some container setups bind only to ::1, which stops the Bazel client from
# reaching its server even though the server is up. Force the IPv4 loopback.
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Djava.net.preferIPv4Stack=true
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Djava.net.preferIPv4Addresses=true
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dsun.net.client.defaultConnectTimeout=30000
# startup --host_jvm_args=-Dsun.net.client.defaultReadTimeout=30000

# --- Local caches -----------------------------------------------------------
# build --disk_cache=~/.cache/bazel-disk
# common --repository_cache=~/.cache/bazel-repo
